Subject: [PATCH 0/9] vkd3d-shader/fx: Support more fx_2_0 state assignment types.

Until now, fx_2_0 state assignments could only be constants. This series adds
the remaining kinds of values that d3dx9 effects use:

  - "compile" expressions, e.g. "VertexShader = compile vs_2_0 vs_main();",
    written as shader objects whose bytecode is stored in the resources
    section;
  - references to parameters, e.g. "Texture = <tex>;" or
    "VertexShader = vs_arr[1];";
  - sampler_state initializers of sampler parameters;
  - TRUE/FALSE for every state;
  - simple expressions over parameters, written as fxlvm code blobs (CTAB,
    CLIT and FXLC sections).

The output was checked by loading it with Wine's d3dx9 (D3DXCreateEffect),
applying the passes, and checking the resulting device states, shaders,
textures and sampler states.

Array selectors (non-constant indices, e.g. "VertexShader = vs_arr[i];"),
matrix expressions and casts from float to integer in expressions are not
supported yet.

chatgptyukkuri (9):
  vkd3d-shader/fx: Introduce a helper to write fx_2_0 data blobs.
  vkd3d-shader/fx: Support writing compile expressions in fx_2_0 state
    assignments.
  vkd3d-shader/fx: Support writing variable references in fx_2_0 state
    assignments.
  vkd3d-shader/fx: Support writing sampler state initializers for
    fx_2_0.
  vkd3d-shader/fx: Accept boolean constants for all fx_2_0 states.
  vkd3d-shader/fx: Write zero element count for fx_2_0 constant state
    values.
  vkd3d-shader/fx: Add the "cmp" fxlc opcode name.
  vkd3d-shader/fx: Support writing simple expressions in fx_2_0 state
    assignments.
  vkd3d-shader/fx: Support more operations in fx_2_0 state expressions.

